<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phalasarna</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Falasarna</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Phalasarna was an ancient Greek harbour city at the western tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>, known for its enclosed artificial harbour, protected by walls and towers. It was a rival of Polyrrhenia and is thought to have served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">pirates</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hellenistic-period">Hellenistic period</a>. Uplift of the land, probably in the great earthquake of 365 CE, raised the harbour about six metres, leaving it now well inland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/phalasarna.jpg" alt="Phalasarna" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Elpida Hadjidaki · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Phalasarna_Round_Tower_Sea.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
